<Project>
  <!-- Pin transitive System.Security.Cryptography.Xml to a patched version.
       Pulled in transitively via FSharp.Compiler.Service / FSharpLint.

       This pin has now moved twice, so record the chain: 9.0.0 was vulnerable
       (GHSA-37gx-xxp4-5rgx, high), which is why the pin existed at all; then
       10.0.9 itself became affected by a second round of high-severity
       advisories whose ranges cover >=10.0.0,<=10.0.9. Patched in 10.0.10.

       Bump this rather than suppressing NU1903 — the warning is doing its job.
       Kept in step with FsHotWatch's identical pin; both consume the same
       FCS/FSharpLint dependency graph, so they go stale together. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
